{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos","id":1376515,"title":"If Archmages aren't a thing in M20 how do you handle say Porthos?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-25T04:47:19-07:00","id":1376515,"title":"If Archmages aren't a thing in M20 how do you handle say Porthos?","content":"So is Porthos just a dude with High Arete and lots of Mastery? How do you handle already established Archmages when we toss out the option of Archmastery? Now they are just Master? Is there anything special about them then? Or do they just practice a lot of rotes and have a lot of Social Clout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T05:56:47-07:00","id":1376531,"title":"","content":"Taking in count how Mage works mechanically.<br /> <br /> Rituals were <b>always </b>the &quot;power source&quot; of mages: This is true for all editions (except, perhaps, 1e - that hasn't very clear ritual rules), and the only limit was and is Paradox and the amount of effects a mage can juggle. Under M20 rules, where the number of non-permanent effects a mage has hanging rarely causes a penalty, an <i>ooooold</i> Archmaster like Vormass, that no longer cares about being perceived by others as a walking magical nuke, could have 100 Coincidental effects casted on himself, with 50+ successes each for no penatly, if you want as ST.<br /> This has the potential to be much more poweful that &quot;doing the same but twice as fast&quot;, becaus even with Arete 9 x 2 you're not going to get, realistically, the 20 + sucesses a ritual can easily net you. And you can still only roll once each turn. (most Archspheres are only powerful if you <i>add </i>them to the existing mechanics, they're rarely <i>that </i>great by themselves)<br /> <br /> Under Revised having a lot of Talismans and Charms (esp. under the rules that allow Talismans to bypass the &quot;one Arete roll per turn&quot;, since they have their own Arete) it's the most powerful boost you can give a Character.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: Archspheres were never what made Porthos a powerful wizard. At least not within pure RAW (if you treat the lvl 6 as a narrative justification for &quot;a power level over 9000&quot;, that's another matter entirely). They were the cherry on top of the already almigthy cake of being a wizard with a lot of clouth <i>in wizard society</i> , and old and wise enough to have better Talismans than anyone else, better Rotes, better pacts with powerful spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> But then what's the difference with other Masters?.<br /> Well, Archspheres may not be <i>a typo</i>, but there's no reason to doubt Word of God when it says that Porthos had 6 because he was supposed to be old'n migthy like elder vampires (and the author folowed the way Vampire does this with &quot;elder Disciplines&quot; , w/o reading the Mage Core first. And would not have given Porthos the lvl 6 if had read the Core first).<br /> <br /> From the begining what made Porthos <b>special </b>was his *age*, and that he was supposed to be badass (Porthos having lvl 6 was an author's mistake). So, yeah, that's the difference. He just has a lot of Arete and it's older and wiser than most, that's why he's best at magic(k) - knowledge (and time) it's power, and all that.<br /> <br /> Btw, this is how he was pretty much represented in the fluff. Porthos it's mentioned in Horison's Forces 6, but you don't ever see him acerting his Archmagedoom by using that level, that &quot;allows a mage to create or influence phenomena for miles around&quot; (that. btw, &quot;demands high dice rolls and advanced preparation&quot; - you don't get to skip rituals. Oh, and Forces 6 didn't allowed in Horizon to cast at Successes x 2, that was an innovation of MotA), in the fluff that covers the rest of the book. He just overpowers other mages, knows how to teleport inside Horizon at will, and uses bizarre Rotes that are &quot;super effective&quot; (the Entropy/Prime/Forces that he used to defeat the guardian spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-25-2020, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:17:02-07:00","id":1376578,"title":"","content":"Outside of one game playing archmages using MotA... Archspheres came up in play exactly... zero times in all my years of playing Mage. Unless the NPC was casting something that the PCs were directly involved in (group casting, targeting them, the PC interrupting a ritual, etc.), I don't even bother rolling for NPC magic the vast majority of the time anyway. If I want Porthos to do something big and awesome with Forces that doesn't mess with player agency, he'll just do it. 5 or 6 dots doesn't really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:25:11-07:00","id":1376581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1376578#post1376578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of one game playing archmages using MotA... Archspheres came up in play exactly... zero times in all my years of playing Mage. Unless the NPC was casting something that the PCs were directly involved in (group casting, targeting them, the PC interrupting a ritual, etc.), I don't even bother rolling for NPC magic the vast majority of the time anyway. If I want Porthos to do something big and awesome with Forces that doesn't mess with player agency, he'll just do it. 5 or 6 dots doesn't really matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters have come up in my games, but the Players don't really fight them, they encounter them and even have them in their Backstories. Big reason not to have them in play as a crunch thing is because you have to houserule a functional system for them. But like Methuselahs and even Antes and Incarna you can have Archmages play a big role in a social situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T11:09:09-07:00","id":1376592,"title":"","content":"Of course, that's why I said Archspheres, not Archmasters. I don't need 6+ ratings in Spheres, or some specific hurdle before a character's an Archmaster to use in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T17:44:52-07:00","id":1376632,"title":"","content":"I wonder how they will handle all archmages of older editions (like Voormas, Medea, the Unnamed)? Maybe like you say, many Masterys, high Arete and huge basical magical dice pool?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1376578#post1376578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of one game playing archmages using MotA... Archspheres came up in play exactly... zero times in all my years of playing Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of this, I think archspehres can work as M20 describes:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rumor has it that levels of Archmastery exist for each Sphere, granting abstract powers that even gods might envy. In game terms, these would be the EXTREMELY optional Sphere Ranks 6-10. <b>Such powers are beyond almost every mage alive, take centuries to attain, and turn chronicles into blasted wreckage.</b> Groups that want to bring such powers into play can find them in the sourcebook Masters of the Art. We cannot, however, overemphasize the destructive potential of these, again, OPTIONAL Sphere Ranks. <b>Though technically canon, they should be avoided for all but the most outlandish Mage chronicles.</b> </div> </div> </div>Just use this description, ignore its recommendation of MotA. That's archspehres in M20, really epic and phenomenal<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1376578#post1376578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If I want Porthos to do something big and awesome with Forces that doesn't mess with player agency, he'll just do it. 5 or 6 dots doesn't really matter. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Plot Device. You can assume almost all effects automatically succeed</span></span></span></div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T18:36:12-07:00","id":1376639,"title":"","content":"Exactly. When you get to archmasters, you're entering the same territory as rank 6 or higher spirits. That is, they're capable of taking on beings that have no stats. and if you are capable of taking on a being that has no stats, then your own stats are largely meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T05:22:30-07:00","id":1376699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1376639#post1376639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and if you are capable of taking on a being that has no stats, then your own stats are largely meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact I think the stats of an archmage is the most meaningless thing. Archmage means EVERYTHING<br /> <br /> But I think portraying them could be simple indeed. More specific rules:<br /> <br /> \u2022 They are methseulah or even antediluvian of mage, remember this<br /> <br /> \u2022 All effects automatically succeed, except truly great ones. Aka. vulgar spells needing 5+ dots or massive successes<br /> \u2022 Give it a huge magical pool if you really need. Mine is roughly 25-50 dices<br /> \u2022 Paradox may be more problematic if you on earth<br /> <br /> \u2022 They are \u201cHoly Grail\u201d everywhere, having great social roles. Everyone of all splats, especially mages and spirits, will stop what they\u2019re doing and listen to them if they just want to have a talk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T06:34:58-07:00","id":1376702,"title":"","content":"Agree and agree. I dont even do stat writes ups for most Masters, much less an Archmage. If I need them to do something they do it. Stats and even sphere level aren't going to stop me. And since they were never written down I never have to fudge the system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T07:11:40-07:00","id":1376706,"title":"","content":"Something else to think about for an Archmage like Porthos who is hundreds of years old. In addition to a high Arete they also will tend to have more than a couple of spheres at 5. Multiple 5 dot spheres can (and often are) greatly more powerful in concert with one another than a single arch sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T20:01:09-07:00","id":1376893,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of the material is that being a really powerful mage isn't just having enough dots on the chart (Arete, spheres, whatever) but also having the mind (knowledge, imagination, wits, experience, etc.) to use their powers effectively/efficiently (maximum results for minimum effort and consequences) - which is in line with what Aleph mentioned (use of Talismans, rituals, influence, etc.) Think along the lines of a memetic 'always have a countermeasure' Batman. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:49:31-07:00","id":1393773,"title":"","content":"In my short try during school I handled it that such Archmages have something like an Aura of Might and Brilliance that make other instinctivly know, you better not mess with them and the Mentor of them just said:&quot;You are still to young for even just watching it.&quot; so yeah until you play with the group decades in RL there is no need for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:26:19-07:00","id":1394061,"title":"","content":"Just to bring it up. Page 68 of M20 mentions that archspheres are technically canon... All the while the book advises you not to use them, of course. <br /> <br /> In my opinion, they are badly written. If you don't want to tack on the rules from those books or make your own spheres from 1 to 9 but must take Sphere level 6 into account. I'd advise you just use Sphere 6 as what let's you go beyond what sphere 5 can do, like jump reality to another dimension, affect the vampire curse, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:42:43-07:00","id":1394120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1394061#post1394061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to bring it up. Page 68 of M20 mentions that archspheres are technically canon... All the while the book advises you not to use them, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not just adviced not to use them, they're stated to be an EXTREMELY <b>optional </b>rule. Note that they weren't optional in Revised nor in 2ed.<br /> <br /> An optional rule's standing within the concept of &quot;canon&quot; it's a bit complex - after all, while part of the bible, disregarding an option it's as much following the canon as taking it in count. A table where Archspheres do not exist isn't using &quot;house rules&quot; at all (that's canon too!).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:53:24-07:00","id":1394125,"title":"","content":"There's nothing stopping anyone from using archspheres if they want to. Personally, I've always seen Porthos's stats as being more of a narrative guide than a hard rule. Porthos is a storyteller character, after all, not a player character, so it's not like the scale really matters that much. <br /> <br /> The stats can be helpful in two ways, though:<br /> <br /> 1. They're a reminder of the character's strengths. Obviously, if I have Porthos do something spectacular to further the plot, I should probably make sure that it's forces related, since that's clearly his strength.<br /> <br /> 2. They can also be a nice little guide on how the NPCs measure up to each other. If I want the players to witness a duel or battle between Porthos and an NPC who has Forces 7-9, then I know that I should portray this as a pretty tough fight in which Porthos might be the underdog, and will have to resort to strategy and cunning if he's supposed to win. <br /> <br /> I'm all for rolling a bunch of dice for dramatic effect, but I think when we're dealing with NPCs of this level, we don't really need that anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:01:41-07:00","id":1394176,"title":"","content":"My initial read of the RAW was that Archspheres were nixed, and I even stated as much to my group. But the other day I discovered the part mentioned in this discussion, where they technically might exists but it is suggested to avoid them. M20 does a lot of that. It *almost* makes a command decision on several things, proposes a new way to do something and states it is now the standard presumption, but then includes a small line or two about how to do it the other way anyways. I *do* like the flexibility, but it takes up space and causes confusion. Still, I would rather have it than not have it.<br /> <br /> So I suppose Arch-Spheres are to be treated as a concept on the background as a potential possibility. As GM tool for world building, intended for NPC's, they do not need in-depth definition. So if the subject ever does come up, I am just gonna stick with ranks six and seven. Six allows you to do those things that were just beyond your reach with standard magic rules and limits. Seven is some omega level shit that you can just fiat.<br /> <br /> Horizon had an Arch Sphere system that went up to seven,and that is the way it works in Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:18:10-07:00","id":1394201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1394061#post1394061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to bring it up. Page 68 of M20 mentions that archspheres are technically canon... All the while the book advises you not to use them, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1394120#post1394120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not just adviced not to use them, they're stated to be an EXTREMELY <b>optional </b>rule. Note that they weren't optional in Revised nor in 2ed.<br /> <br /> An optional rule's standing within the concept of &quot;canon&quot; it's a bit complex - after all, while part of the bible, disregarding an option it's as much following the canon as taking it in count. A table where Archspheres do not exist isn't using &quot;house rules&quot; at all (that's canon too!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to be more blunt: Brucato has been vocal of his dislike for Archspheres, because he really-really does not like high power/cosmic tier Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:41:18-07:00","id":1394207,"title":"","content":"It's not just about not liking high power levels; it's also that the five Sphere levels in the core book are already deep into the \u201chigh power level\u201d tier, and doesn't leave much if any room for the sixth dot to mean anything. To the extent that Brucato accepts that a sixth dot should be allowed in the game at all, the philosophy appears to be that it should be nearly impossible to attain, and should largely be defined in terms of what the Storyteller wishes to forbid mages from doing. <br /> <br /> And if you don't want to put any upper limits on what mages can do, you don't need the Archspheres; just allow everything to be done with five dots or less. Remember, Magickal Feats include Outlandish and God-like Feats, too. <br /> <br /> As I recall, <b>Horizon: Stronghold of Hope</b> was written with this mindset. By contrast, <b>Masters of the Art</b> was written with the notion that there ought to be nine dots in every Sphere, and that player characters ought to be able to continue the progression all the way up to 9 in the same way they progressed from 1 to 5: get a sufficiently high Arete and spend 7\u00d7 or 8\u00d7 the new rank in the Sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:27:33-07:00","id":1394214,"title":"","content":"I didn't like the archspheres as written so I made the following as my version of archspheres, more to figure out what an archmage game might be like than anything else. <br /> <br /> Correspondence<br /> 6: Correspondence can be used to access unconnected worlds and realms of existence <br /> 7: Wards, environmental effects, and other similar hindrances to perception or travel can be ignored<br /> 8: The Mage can perceives &amp; reach everything in the same world or realm of existence<br /> 9: All is one. Obstacles and barriers are suggestions<br /> Entropy <br /> 6: Entropy can be frozen or reversed. Fate may be predetermined and sealed<br /> 7: Things can be removed from fate (retroactively annihilated, severed from history, or made \u201cArcane\u201d)<br /> 8: Things like destinies &amp; binding oaths may be reversed, redirected, transferred, altered, or removed<br /> 9: The irreversible can be reversed, irresistible resisted, immovable moved, and unbreakable broken<br /> Forces<br /> 6: New kinds of minor forces may be invented that directly affect Correspondence, Life or Matter<br /> 7: New kinds of minor forces may be invented that directly affect Spirit or Mind<br /> 8: New kinds of minor forces may be invented that directly affect Entropy, Prime, or Time<br /> 9: New kinds of major forces may be invented that can affect any of the Spheres<br /> Life<br /> 6: Reality defying creatures of legend with and their qualities become accessible to the mage without need for other spheres<br /> 7: Dynamic systems of Spirit, Force or Matter can be treated as life<br /> 8: Anything that can grow, change, evolve, or die off can be treated as life<br /> 9: All of reality is alive in a way and falls under the purview of the Life sphere<br /> Matter<br /> 6: Forces and Life can be treated as Matter<br /> 7: Correspondence, Prime &amp; Spirit can be treated as Matter<br /> 8: Mind, Entropy &amp; Time can be treated as Matter<br /> 9: All of reality can be treated as Matter<br /> Mind <br /> 6: The universal subconscious becomes a valid target for Mind <br /> 7: Thoughts can be converted into reality<br /> 8: Real things can be made imaginary<br /> 9: Everything is information contained within a single supreme consciousness<br /> Prime <br /> 6: Paradox can be predicted, transferred, and manipulated<br /> 7: The Mage can perceive &amp; understand all supernatural powers and can suppress, redirect, or counter these<br /> 8: Quintessence can be created from nothing. Personal Quintessence can be stolen<br /> 9: The laws of magic can be bent, broken, appended or rewritten<br /> Spirit<br /> 6: New Souls and Spirits up to the level of a Seraphim, Praeceptor, or Demigod can be easily created or remade (with 1 success)<br /> 7: An Avatar can be created and Awakening can be forced or reversed. <br /> 8: The Mage can easily make or become a spiritual incarnation of a concept or thing, like a Totem, Archangel, or Demon lord<br /> 9: The Mage can easily make or become something just short of the Essential Divinity, equivalent to a Godhead or Celestine<br /> Time<br /> 6: The mage can access the Coming or Previous \u201cAge\u201d such as one of the Impossible Futures or Mythic Ages <br /> 7: The mage can access parallel timelines, difficulty based on how far back the divergence was<br /> 8: The mage can reshape an entire timeline, rewriting events therein, connecting it to a desired future, or even looping it<br /> 9: The mage can access and reshape all of time of all ages and realms<br /> <br /> Its a bit off in points, looking at it now, but easily &quot;corrected&quot;, not that I found much point in doing so after a bit of hypothetical use. <br /> <br /> I soon decided that old replaced timelines branched off every time new ones were made so sometimes an archmage seemed to simply vanish when desiring to live in a different timeline.<br /> <br /> These days I'd just rather that each dot above 5 lowered the difficulty of use of that sphere by 1 or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:49:52-07:00","id":1394453,"title":"","content":"I do the quick and dirty with the Forces 6 from MOTA and just apply that. I think it's an important enough inclusion to take into account that makes Archmages very powerful but gives them a decent enough guideline that you can still counter them with the correct resources (and luck)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T23:32:58-07:00","id":1394729,"title":"","content":"Somewhere on an old website in the 90s, the suggestion was that Arete 6-10 gave corresponding bonuses for Sphere effects five dots lower. So the guy with Arete 6 has super senses, but the mage with Arete 10 can pop of Sphere 5 effects like candy.<br /> <br /> And by bonuses - I mean, they &quot;cast&quot; a certain level of effect below say, a threshhold of their Arete without even trying. Or something like that. So an Arete 10 Mage is terrifying - they can cast a 9 successes Sphere 5 effect without even rolling. This makes &quot;Archmages&quot; powerful, but without Archspheres. It all depends on what the ST wants Arete 6+ mages capable of in their chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 06-07-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:44:03-07:00","id":1394812,"title":"","content":"I just remembered. Horizon stronghold of hope had its own method of handling sphere level 6 detailed in page 117.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:54:32-07:00","id":1394819,"title":"","content":"If I get bored and a player asks me what sphere six does if they get it, I might just tell them:<br /> <br /> They get to choose between MOA and Horizon rules and that one choice leads to personal ascension while the other does not \ud83d\ude06","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T00:50:49-07:00","id":1395542,"title":"","content":"I won't give mage archspheres <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When levels of a power are many, it is very difficult to level it appropriately. </span></span></span></div> <br /> I don't know how many of you tried writing a powers having 10 levels from the scratch. I used to do it, and it's... messy<br /> And Vampire's Disciplines of the old version is an example, when comes to elder disciplines the power level is a bit confused, some 6 dots ones can crush 9 dots ones down, etc. No wonder authorites removed the whole 6+ traits in 5E, which proves my theory in some ways<br /> <br /> Needless to say mage don't really need something like &quot;elder spheres&quot;, MtA is very different from VtM<br /> <br /> From this perspective, V5 is on the right way. Elder and Methseulah powers can be represented as potent combo disciplines demanding high Blood Potency, 6+ traits don't need exist, too, add some special backgrounds on your dice pool is not a bad idea (just like Ancestor of WtA)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-10-2020, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T00:58:00-07:00","id":1395543,"title":"","content":"I think keeping things limited to 5 encourages trying to find fancier/hidden styles of magic to accomplish 'impossible' tasks, using more sphere knowledge, more ritual.<br /> Though I'm not entirely against arch-spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T01:02:30-07:00","id":1395544,"title":"","content":"When the levels of a power is 5, no problem, M20 is an exemplar <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When the levels of a power is 6-7, not that bad, you make 6 dots Plot Device when it has six levels, and make 6 dots &quot;limited Plot Device&quot;, 7 dots &quot;true PD&quot; when it has seven levels<br /> But when the levels is 10... come on, man. &quot;10&quot; should be an ultimate summit in D10, how to set it?<br /> And 6-9 dots?<br /> And 6-9 dots traits? To be honest I can't imagine how should they work? Apperance 6-10 are the same to me<br /> <br /> VtM used to try to write 10 dots powers in earlier editions, and that's bad. See Player's Guide 1st and 2nd, you won't believe they're level 10 powers. The latest ones are Daimonion 10 in Baali book and Valeren 10 in Salubri book, both of which are also a bit old materials<br /> Then they became smarter, avoiding these mines, just writing level 9 powers at most. At last threw a &quot;Plot Device&quot; in Gehenna</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-10-2020, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:33:04-07:00","id":1395555,"title":"","content":"I don't think they ever wrote sphere level 10s<br /> <br /> And the sphere level 6 option in horizon in my opinion seems to be the sanest cannon approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:35:23-07:00","id":1395556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1395555#post1395555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they ever wrote sphere level 10s<br /> <br /> And the sphere level 6 option in horizon in my opinion seems to be the sanest cannon approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 10-level DO exist in Revised edition<br /> They just didn't really write this foolishly, a lesson learned from VtM<br /> Even before the Unnamed sheet in Ascension, some books also imply this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:50:24-07:00","id":1395557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1395556#post1395556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 10-level DO exist in Revised edition<br /> They just didn't really write this foolishly, a lesson learned from VtM<br /> Even before the Unnamed sheet in Ascension, some books also imply this</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only read to 9. What does 10 in correspondence do for example?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or are you talking about that thing where you become an avatar of the sphere by getting it at 10?<br /> <br /> I don't really consider that a rating but okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 06-10-2020, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:54:14-07:00","id":1395558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1395557#post1395557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've only read to 9. What does 10 in correspondence do for example?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or are you talking about that thing where you become an avatar if the sphere by getting it at 10?<br /> <br /> I don't really consider that a rating but okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had said they didn't really write 10s' effects, but they do exist<br /> <br /> See Unnamed in Ascension, Entropy 10<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Unnamed</b><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Faction</b>: <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/K%27llasshaa