r /> Backgrounds: Allies 5, Arcane 5, <b>Avatar (variable: 4 when totally sane to 9 (!) when totally insane)</b>, Destiny 3, Dream 3<br /> <br /> Spheres: Variable basedonsanity. The more insane, the more powerful.) Entropy 2-4, Forces 3-4, Life 2-4, Mind 3-4, Prime 2, Spirit 2-4 </div> </div> </div>But it's a very early book, you should know early material usually has crazy stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-12-2020, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T06:52:14-07:00","id":1396014,"title":"","content":"Arete specifically goes up to 10 in M20. I'm pretty sure I never saw it stated it can't go above 5 in earlier editions.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm blind. I read avatar as Arete","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 06-12-2020, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T07:49:24-07:00","id":1396018,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> so Archmages no longer exist in the post-Avatar Storm universe or they exist but they\u2019re all beyond the First Horizon?<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking about buying Masters of the Art. Is there stuff about Archmages in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:02:16-07:00","id":1396020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396018#post1396018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> so Archmages no longer exist in the post-Avatar Storm universe or they exist but they\u2019re all beyond the First Horizon?<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking about buying Masters of the Art. Is there stuff about Archmages in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. As far as is known. They're all stuck. Masters of the art details archmages. I'd check out Horizon as well for the NPCs and social aspect. Though Masters of the Art is specifically about archmagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:10:13-07:00","id":1396024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396018#post1396018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> so Archmages no longer exist in the post-Avatar Storm universe or they exist but they\u2019re all beyond the First Horizon?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very small number of Archmages survived Avatar Storm and stayed on Earth (Primus Ishaq Ibn-Thoth, Revised OoH), some were destroyed, some were stuck at Umbra( Infinite Tapestry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:18:44-07:00","id":1396026,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T10:11:04-07:00","id":1396038,"title":"","content":"If I recall the person who had Avatar 10 was straight up eating Mages and that was the explanation for it, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T10:52:29-07:00","id":1396042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396038#post1396038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall the person who had Avatar 10 was straight up eating Mages and that was the explanation for it, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c10\u201d is an ultimate summit in D10, but in system it just means you can regain 10 Quintessence at once, etc<br /> <br /> Arete 10 also only means you have 10 rolls in basical magick pool and is relatively poor, even if you don\u2019t compare it with other same-level splats (F**k, older editions suck)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-12-2020, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:17:27-07:00","id":1396238,"title":"","content":"Personally I think Imperial Mysteries from Awakening has the idea of arch powers right. They break the rules in a methodical fashion that promotes a story of engaging with or fighting against. Want to cure the curse of caine? Arch spheres. Want to unflip a nephandi. archsphere. Every sphere effect in arch spheres are a game breaking, redefining story.<br /> <br /> But they are also really hard to do even if you have the spheres, you need particular things, at times and other arch mages want those limited resources do theirown miracles...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:43:17-07:00","id":1396243,"title":"","content":"If they have to be used at all, I think Horizon is a much more elegant and overall better approach. But I favor keeping all conceivable effects under the umbrella of 5 dots, with number of successes required distinguishing the truly legendary feats. And considering someone an archmage if they have Arete 6+ and multiple Spheres at 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:37:13-07:00","id":1396378,"title":"","content":"@Mattthebruinsfan would you recommend I buy both Horizon and Masters of the Art if I want info on Archmages in Mage: the Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T07:14:37-07:00","id":1396673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396243#post1396243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have to be used at all, I think Horizon is a much more elegant and overall better approach. But I favor keeping all conceivable effects under the umbrella of 5 dots, with number of successes required distinguishing the truly legendary feats. And considering someone an archmage if they have Arete 6+ and multiple Spheres at 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this as well. MOTA, IMO has many of the 6+ sphere effects to an almost comical level. If you feel you must represent an archmage as someone having more than a 6+ Arete then I'd use Horizon rules and just umbrella all the MOTA ideas for sphere ability under sphere rank 6 capabilities. <br /> <br /> Basically saying that sphere ratings of 6 allow for anything not allowed by the lower sphere levels and regulate from there with success requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T07:39:43-07:00","id":1396678,"title":"","content":"I wasn't the one asked, but I think Masters of the Art is a good book for flavor, especially in conjunction with the Initiates book. I think it can be really helpful in helping a storyteller decide exactly how archmages fit into the dynamics of the story. And as silly as the archspheres are, I think they do provide some decent inspiration on how you might want to showcase the power of the character.<br /> <br /> So if you have the money for both Masters and Horizon, then I'd recommend getting both. If you only have the money for one, and/or you're mostly just interested in a workable set of rules, then I'd go with Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T15:01:56-07:00","id":1396737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396378#post1396378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Mattthebruinsfan would you recommend I buy both Horizon and Masters of the Art if I want info on Archmages in Mage: the Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say if you can afford both get them to compare, contrast, and decide which you prefer. But if you're only going to get one Horizon would be my recommendation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T19:00:43-07:00","id":1396777,"title":"","content":"Bah, MotA is bad but Horizon system is somewhat cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T19:01:01-07:00","id":1396778,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> thank you \ud83d\ude0a. Imma get both.<br /> <br /> I guess my only concern would be is the Horizon book still relevant in the default M20 setting in which the Avatar Storm has already happened and Horizon is left in ruins. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T19:05:03-07:00","id":1396780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26165_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26165\" data-vbnamecard=\"26165\">GothicxXx</a> your screen name reminds me of a funny story that happened to me at my first job.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for your recommendation. But can you answer the question I posted above? I just don\u2019t wanna buy a book that\u2019ll be basically useless if I (or my ST) end up using the Avatar Storm plotline. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T20:37:21-07:00","id":1396796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396778#post1396778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> thank you \ud83d\ude0a. Imma get both.<br /> <br /> I guess my only concern would be is the Horizon book still relevant in the default M20 setting in which the Avatar Storm has already happened and Horizon is left in ruins. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, much of Horizon as a setting book won't be of use except maybe if players want to try and find the remains of horizon and you are running a game about something like finding the old council or what remains of them. <br /> <br /> What it does contain is a good simple set of rules for archmages and a clear idea of what archmages might have been like. So if your game is nearing the Arete 6 level, that little section in the back of the book might be good for you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Masters of the art is really all about archmages, immortality rotes, and crazy high level mage games <br /> stuff of the type that you normally have to change your mindset to run properly. <br /> <br /> The system for archspheres there is clunky in comparison and best for long out of this world archmages campaigns for players who like lots of rules and levels of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:14:01-07:00","id":1396801,"title":"","content":"Horizons gives a nice peak at the peak of Tradition's culture and civilization and how their Archmages made their own world and home. I need to reread it again, at least the archsphere part because I think it probably works better as an Archsphere rather then a 6-10 level range of Archspheres.<br /> <br /> Masters of the Arts gave interesting looks at multiple options for how Mages wind up when they keep growing in power but don't ascend, like Exemplars living embodiments of their strongest Sphere and things like Archmages taking Gods like Incarnae and even the Celestines as mentors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T03:34:24-07:00","id":1396844,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Thanks. Yeah, I\u2019m defo gonna buy both and see which one I like better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T03:09:47-07:00","id":1397039,"title":"","content":"I like the fluff in MotA and the mechanics in Horizon \u2014 though these days, my preference is to define archmastery in terms of Feats rather than Spheres. That is, instead of talking about Sphere level 6, I'm more inclined to talk about godlike Feats (20+ successes in the RAW).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T21:51:32-07:00","id":1397448,"title":"","content":"I really feel Horizon and MotA take different approaches to the same outcome. Horizon is a more narrative approach (the limits are less broadly defined and more storyteller/story based) whereas MotA puts more game mechanics around the limits (and more detail). Both can be game breaking, but I feel that the way they handle the character development is perhaps most different. A 'Horizon' inspired archmage still feels like a human being more or less. Whereas MotA seems to depict something that becomes less human the further it progresses. Similar outcomes but different routes and different costs. And as others mentioned I liked the Awakening approach to such things as well (there's a lot I like about Mage the Awakening's magic system actually, and I do borrow shamelessly from it if I want. Of course I also like Dark Age Mage's approach...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T13:42:44-07:00","id":1403709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1397039#post1397039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the fluff in MotA and the mechanics in Horizon \u2014 though these days, my preference is to define archmastery in terms of Feats rather than Spheres. That is, instead of talking about Sphere level 6, I'm more inclined to talk about godlike Feats (20+ successes in the RAW).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would handle Archspheres more like Imperium Rites in <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> than &quot;scaled up conventional magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T13:47:32-07:00","id":1403711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1403709#post1403709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I would handle Archspheres more like Imperium Rites in <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> than &amp;quot;scaled up conventional magic&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a huge fan of Imperial Mysteries, that is why I wished Malcolm got tapped to do Archapheres for M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T00:53:41-07:00","id":1403769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1396780#post1396780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26165_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26165\" data-vbnamecard=\"26165\">GothicxXx</a> your screen name reminds me of a funny story that happened to me at my first job.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for your recommendation. But can you answer the question I posted above? I just don\u2019t wanna buy a book that\u2019ll be basically useless if I (or my ST) end up using the Avatar Storm plotline. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to actually buy the book, you can try to find in Google some article that goes strictly into the functionality of the 6 dot spheres on Horizon book as you not planning to use the whole book, mostly of them become &quot;AoE&quot; effects, wich you can manipulate multiple patterns at the same time without dividing sucess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T03:10:41-07:00","id":1403785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376515-if-archmages-aren-t-a-thing-in-m20-how-do-you-handle-say-porthos?p=1403769#post1403769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to actually buy the book, you can try to find in Google some article that goes strictly into the functionality of the 6 dot spheres on Horizon book as you not planning to use the whole book, mostly of them become &amp;quot;AoE&amp;quot; effects, wich you can manipulate multiple patterns at the same time without dividing sucess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}